# Docs site source
!docs/
!docs/**
!docs/**/*.json
!docs/.gitignore
!.github/
!.github/**
.claude/

# ...but a secret is still a secret inside them. The two blanket re-includes
# above are the LAST rules to match anything under docs/ or .github/, and the
# last match wins -- so they quietly cancelled the `.env*` and `proxies.txt`
# rules for those two trees, and `git check-ignore docs/.env` answered
# "!docs/**". docs/ is a Vite project, and a Vite project's root is exactly
# where its documented `.env` goes, so the hole sat directly under the one
# place someone would put a token. (docs/.gitignore's `*.local` caught
# docs/.env.local and nothing else, which is what made it easy to miss.)
# Restated here so they win again.
.env*
!.env.example
proxies.txt

# Data, not source. All of it stays on disk -- this only stops it going to
# GitHub, where it is large, machine-specific, or both.
*.parquet
data/missing_unrecoverable/
# undo journals: hundreds of KB of absolute paths from THIS machine
runs/*.json
# the dnd env was abandoned for yolo; its lockfile documents nothing live
data/dnd_env_lock.txt

# generated review thumbnails (rebuilt on demand from the originals)
data/dashboard/hq_crops/
data/dashboard/sequence_cache.json

# Dashboard: the module is committed, its machine-specific settings are not.
# ('*/' above already hides these; naming them is the durable guarantee, and
# tools/detect/tests/adv_no_hardcoded_paths.py fails the build if a path
# leaks back into the committed files.)
tools/dashboard/dashboard.config.json
tools/dashboard/street-dogs-dashboard.service

# One-off hardware remediation for THIS host: device nodes (/dev/sdm, /dev/sdd),
# a drive serial and USB bridge ids. Named individually rather than globbed --
# a `fix_*.sh` pattern would silently swallow a future script that belonged in
# the repo.
fix_bobcat_mount.sh
fix_lynx_spindown.sh

# model suggestions for the review filter -- never training data, and
# regenerable from tools/detect/triage_crops.py
data/dashboard/triage.jsonl
data/labelstudio_frames/

# The built dashboard page. Generated, and it embeds absolute paths
# from whichever machine built it.
data/dashboard/index.html
